{
  "_note": "Open-weight IMAGE and VIDEO generation models, newest first. Every parameter count here was derived from the ACTUAL staged weights (safetensors shard sizes and safetensors headers read out of ThakiCloud's s3://ai-platform/global/models registry) divided by the on-disk dtype — not from press material. Component split is backbone (UNet/DiT) / text encoder / VAE-and-aux, because for diffusion the text encoder is often a third of resident VRAM and gets forgotten in back-of-envelope sizing. `measured` rows are OUR OWN single-B200 benchmark runs (2026-08, batch 1, eager bf16, no torch.compile); models without one are marked estimated and the UI says so. Diffusion is COMPUTE bound, not bandwidth bound: there is no KV cache, every denoising step is a full forward over all latent tokens, and batching is nearly worthless (measured: Qwen-Image 2.51 -> 2.37 s/img for VRAM 58 -> 87GB). Quantisation is modelled as a VRAM saving only, never a speedup, because our measurement shows fp8 ALONE is slower (FLUX.2-klein 0.83x) and only wins when fused with torch.compile (1.72x). `catalog: true` = present in the ThakiCloud demo model catalog (project ai-platform).",
